CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*data)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct cycle_trig_data)...)
#610: FILE: drivers/leds/trigger/ledtrig-cycle.c:402:
+	data = kzalloc(sizeof(struct cycle_trig_data), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

